# Try the API by hand: click "Send Request" above each request (VS Code REST Client
# extension, or Visual Studio / Rider). Start the app first with: dotnet run --project Blackjack.Api
@host = http://localhost:5098

### 1. Sign up. Copy "token" from the response into @token below.
POST {{host}}/api/players
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Alice" }

###
@token = paste-token-here

### 2. Your profile, balance, and any round in progress
GET {{host}}/api/players/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. Deal a round with a $25 bet. Note the dealer's second card is null (face-down).
POST {{host}}/api/rounds
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bet": 25 }

###
@roundId = 1

### 4. Hit
POST {{host}}/api/rounds/{{roundId}}/hit
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Stand (the dealer plays out the rest on the server)
POST {{host}}/api/rounds/{{roundId}}/stand
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Wallet balance and audit trail
GET {{host}}/api/wallet
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Refill (only allowed when you're out of chips)
POST {{host}}/api/wallet/refill
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. Leaderboard (no sign-in needed)
GET {{host}}/api/leaderboard?top=10

### 9. Cheating attempt: no token, so this is rejected with 401
POST {{host}}/api/rounds
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bet": 25 }
